    "intro_html":  "Lok lak means to shake, which is what you do to the pan while the beef sears. Cambodia\u0027s version leans hard on black pepper, and Kampot pepper from the southern coast is what makes people write love letters about this dish. Beef gets marinated in oyster sauce and soy, seared fast and hard, then piled over rice with tomato and red onion. Lime juice goes over the top at the end. Fast, sharp, and completely unlike anything else in our library.",
