    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eThe beef is the entire cost of this dish.\u003c/strong\u003e Buy steak when the case marks it down and freeze it. Slicing it thin means a smaller amount goes a long way per bowl.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eFreeze the steak thirty minutes before slicing.\u003c/strong\u003e Firm meat slices thin with a regular knife, and thin slices sear in seconds instead of stewing in their own juice.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBlack pepper is the star, so grind it fresh.\u003c/strong\u003e Pre-ground pepper has already lost most of what makes this dish worth making, and a peppermill pays for itself fast.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eOyster sauce and kecap manis are two bottles that keep for months.\u003c/strong\u003e They are what give the marinade its depth, and they cost pennies per batch once they are in your pantry."
